### IntelliJ HTTP Client - open this file and click the green arrow next to a request.
### Start the app first (port 8080). Seed data: books 1-4, members 1-2.

### List books (search + paging)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books?q=clean&page=0&size=10

### Create a book
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "isbn": "9780596007126",
  "title": "Head First Design Patterns",
  "author": "Eric Freeman",
  "category": "Software Design",
  "totalCopies": 2
}

### Create a member
POST http://localhost:8080/api/members
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Nasrin Sultana",
  "email": "nasrin@example.com",
  "phone": "01900000003"
}

### Borrow book 1 as member 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/borrowings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "bookId": 1,
  "memberId": 1
}

### Return borrow record 1 (fine is calculated if late)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/borrowings/1/return

### Pay the fine of record 1
POST http://localhost:8080/api/borrowings/1/pay-fine

### All currently borrowed books
GET http://localhost:8080/api/borrowings?status=BORROWED

### Overdue books
GET http://localhost:8080/api/borrowings/overdue

### Member's borrowing history
GET http://localhost:8080/api/borrowings/member/1

### Member's unpaid fines
GET http://localhost:8080/api/borrowings/member/1/fines
